§ `Cases`

§§ `s 6 -- spouse`

-- s 6(1)(a): legally married on the commencement date.
#ASSERT `Is this person my spouse for the grant` TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- s 6(2): legally married, but the Chief Commissioner is satisfied they were not cohabiting and will not resume.
#ASSERT (NOT (`Is this person my spouse for the grant` TRUE FALSE TRUE))
-- s 6(1)(b): a de facto partner.
#ASSERT `Is this person my spouse for the grant` FALSE TRUE FALSE
-- Neither.
#ASSERT (NOT (`Is this person my spouse for the grant` FALSE FALSE FALSE))

§§ `s 4A -- new home`

-- s 4A(1): an off-the-plan apartment never occupied or sold as a place of residence.
#ASSERT `Is my home a new home` `neither renovated nor built to replace demolished premises` FALSE FALSE
-- s 4A(1): an established home, lived in before.
#ASSERT (NOT (`Is my home a new home` `neither renovated nor built to replace demolished premises` TRUE FALSE))
-- s 4A(2): a substantially renovated home not occupied or sold since the renovation.
#ASSERT `Is my home a new home` `a substantially renovated home` FALSE FALSE
-- s 4A(3)(c): a knock-down rebuild where the owner lived in the old house (READING: (3)(c) applies; finding 3).
#ASSERT (NOT (`Is my home a new home` `a home built to replace demolished premises on the same land` FALSE TRUE))
-- s 4A(3): a rebuild where the owner never lived in the old house.
#ASSERT `Is my home a new home` `a home built to replace demolished premises on the same land` FALSE FALSE

§§ `s 5 -- relevant interest`

-- s 5(2)(a), (3): freehold, with a right to move in within 12 months, not on trust.
#ASSERT `Is my interest a relevant interest` `an estate in fee simple` TRUE FALSE
-- s 5(3)(b): held subject to a trust.
#ASSERT (NOT (`Is my interest a relevant interest` `an estate in fee simple` TRUE TRUE))
-- s 5(3)(a): no right to immediate occupation within 12 months (a long lease to a tenant, say).
#ASSERT (NOT (`Is my interest a relevant interest` `an estate in fee simple` FALSE FALSE))
-- s 5(2)(e1): a purchaser under a terms contract.
#ASSERT `Is my interest a relevant interest` `a purchaser's interest in fee simple under a terms contract` TRUE FALSE
-- s 5(2): an ordinary lease is not in the list.
#ASSERT (NOT (`Is my interest a relevant interest` `some other interest, such as an ordinary lease or a tenancy` TRUE FALSE))

§§ `s 15 -- other owners`

-- Every owner applies.
#ASSERT `Can my application go ahead without the other owners` 0 0
-- s 15(2)(e): one parent with 5% does not apply; the only small interest holder.
#ASSERT `Can my application go ahead without the other owners` 5 5
-- s 15(2)(e): two parents with 3% each do not apply; small interest holders total 6%, so neither is excluded.
#ASSERT (NOT (`Can my application go ahead without the other owners` 3 6))
-- Two parents with 2% each: total 4%.
#ASSERT `Can my application go ahead without the other owners` 2 4
-- s 15(1): a sibling with 10% must apply.
#ASSERT (NOT (`Can my application go ahead without the other owners` 10 0))

§§ `s 13 -- eligible transaction`

-- s 13(1)(a): Jess's contract of 1 March 2024 for a new home in New South Wales.
#ASSERT `Is my transaction an eligible transaction` `a contract for the purchase of a home` TRUE `1 Mar 2024` `neither renovated nor built to replace demolished premises` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE `it replaces no earlier contract` EQUALS `answered` TRUE
-- s 13(1)(a): made on 1 October 2012 itself.
#ASSERT `Is my transaction an eligible transaction` `a contract for the purchase of a home` TRUE `1 Oct 2012` `neither renovated nor built to replace demolished premises` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE `it replaces no earlier contract` EQUALS `answered` TRUE
-- Schedule 1 cl 18: a contract made on 30 September 2012 is under the earlier Part 2, not deposited: not covered.
#ASSERT `Is my transaction an eligible transaction` `a contract for the purchase of a home` TRUE `30 Sep 2012` `neither renovated nor built to replace demolished premises` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE `it replaces no earlier contract` EQUALS `not covered` `the commencement date is before 1 October 2012, and Schedule 1 Part 11 keeps the earlier Part 2, which is not deposited`
-- s 13(1)(a): a home in Queensland.
#ASSERT `Is my transaction an eligible transaction` `a contract for the purchase of a home` FALSE `1 Mar 2024` `neither renovated nor built to replace demolished premises` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE `it replaces no earlier contract` EQUALS `answered` FALSE
-- s 13(1)(a), s 4A: an established home.
#ASSERT `Is my transaction an eligible transaction` `a contract for the purchase of a home` TRUE `1 Mar 2024` `neither renovated nor built to replace demolished premises` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE `it replaces no earlier contract` EQUALS `answered` FALSE
-- s 13(1)(b): a building contract made by someone who neither owns nor will own the land.
#ASSERT `Is my transaction an eligible transaction` `a comprehensive home building contract` TRUE `1 Mar 2024` `neither renovated nor built to replace demolished premises` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `it replaces no earlier contract` EQUALS `answered` FALSE
-- s 13(1)(c): an owner build on the builder's own land.
#ASSERT `Is my transaction an eligible transaction` `the building of a home by an owner builder` TRUE `1 Mar 2024` `neither renovated nor built to replace demolished premises` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE `it replaces no earlier contract` EQUALS `answered` TRUE
-- s 13(3): a contract under an option granted before 1 July 2000.
#ASSERT `Is my transaction an eligible transaction` `a contract for the purchase of a home` TRUE `1 Mar 2024` `neither renovated nor built to replace demolished premises` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE `it replaces no earlier contract` EQUALS `answered` FALSE
-- s 13(3A), Schedule 1 cl 19: it replaces a contract made before 1 October 2012: not covered.
#ASSERT `Is my transaction an eligible transaction` `a contract for the purchase of a home` TRUE `1 Mar 2024` `neither renovated nor built to replace demolished premises` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE `it replaces a contract made before 1 October 2012` EQUALS `not covered` `the Chief Commissioner is satisfied the contract replaces one made before 1 July 2017, and Schedule 1 keeps the earlier law, which is not encoded`

§§ `s 13AA -- which grant`

-- s 13AA(3): a purchase gets the purchaser's grant; (2): building gets the builder's grant.
#ASSERT `Which grant is available for my transaction` `a contract for the purchase of a home` EQUALS `a first home purchaser's grant`
#ASSERT `Which grant is available for my transaction` `a comprehensive home building contract` EQUALS `a first home builder's grant`
#ASSERT `Which grant is available for my transaction` `the building of a home by an owner builder` EQUALS `a first home builder's grant`

§§ `s 13A -- the eligibility cap`

-- s 13A(2)(b): $600,000 for a purchaser's grant; (a) $750,000 for a builder's grant.
#ASSERT `What is the eligibility cap for my transaction` `a contract for the purchase of a home` `1 Mar 2024` `it replaces no earlier contract` FALSE 0 EQUALS `answered` 600000
#ASSERT `What is the eligibility cap for my transaction` `a comprehensive home building contract` `10 Feb 2025` `it replaces no earlier contract` FALSE 0 EQUALS `answered` 750000
#ASSERT `What is the eligibility cap for my transaction` `the building of a home by an owner builder` `10 Feb 2025` `it replaces no earlier contract` FALSE 0 EQUALS `answered` 750000
-- s 13A(5): the section applies from a commencement date of 1 July 2017.
#ASSERT `What is the eligibility cap for my transaction` `a contract for the purchase of a home` `1 Jul 2017` `it replaces no earlier contract` FALSE 0 EQUALS `answered` 600000
-- s 13A(5), Schedule 1 cl 22(1): 30 June 2017 is under the earlier caps: not covered.
#ASSERT `What is the eligibility cap for my transaction` `a contract for the purchase of a home` `30 Jun 2017` `it replaces no earlier contract` FALSE 0 EQUALS `not covered` `the commencement date is before 1 July 2017, and Schedule 1 keeps the earlier eligibility caps, which are not encoded`
-- s 13A(4): a regulation's cap, given as an input.
#ASSERT `What is the eligibility cap for my transaction` `a contract for the purchase of a home` `1 Mar 2024` `it replaces no earlier contract` TRUE 650000 EQUALS `answered` 650000
-- s 13A(4): a regulation whose amount is not known: not covered.
#ASSERT `What is the eligibility cap for my transaction` `a contract for the purchase of a home` `1 Mar 2024` `it replaces no earlier contract` TRUE 0 EQUALS `not covered` `a regulation under s 13A(4) sets a different eligibility cap, and its amount was not given (no regulation is deposited)`
-- Schedule 1 cl 22(2): it replaces a contract made before 1 July 2017: not covered.
#ASSERT `What is the eligibility cap for my transaction` `a contract for the purchase of a home` `1 Mar 2024` `it replaces a contract made from 1 October 2012 to 30 June 2017` FALSE 0 EQUALS `not covered` `the Chief Commissioner is satisfied the contract replaces one made before 1 July 2017, and Schedule 1 keeps the earlier law, which is not encoded`

§§ `s 13B -- total value`

-- s 13B(1)(a): a purchase is the greater of the price ($590,000) and the unencumbered value ($605,000).
#ASSERT `What is the total value of my transaction` `a contract for the purchase of a home` 590000 605000 0 0 EQUALS 605000
-- s 13B(1)(b), (2): building price $330,000 plus the land at the greater of $400,000 paid and $420,000 value.
#ASSERT `What is the total value of my transaction` `a comprehensive home building contract` 330000 0 400000 420000 EQUALS 750000
-- s 13B(1)(c), (2): an owner build: the home's value at completion ($500,000) plus the land (greater of $200,000 and
-- $260,000); the owner builder's costs ($300,000) do not count.
#ASSERT `What is the total value of my transaction` `the building of a home by an owner builder` 300000 500000 200000 260000 EQUALS 760000

§§ `ss 7(1)(c), 13A -- within the cap`

-- $750,000 does not exceed the $750,000 cap.
#ASSERT `Is my transaction within the cap` `a comprehensive home building contract` `10 Feb 2025` `it replaces no earlier contract` 330000 0 400000 420000 FALSE 0 EQUALS `answered` TRUE
-- $751,000 does.
#ASSERT `Is my transaction within the cap` `a comprehensive home building contract` `10 Feb 2025` `it replaces no earlier contract` 330000 0 400000 421000 FALSE 0 EQUALS `answered` FALSE
-- The owner build at $760,000 is over; with the land at $240,000 it is $740,000 and under.
#ASSERT `Is my transaction within the cap` `the building of a home by an owner builder` `10 Feb 2025` `it replaces no earlier contract` 300000 500000 200000 260000 FALSE 0 EQUALS `answered` FALSE
#ASSERT `Is my transaction within the cap` `the building of a home by an owner builder` `10 Feb 2025` `it replaces no earlier contract` 300000 500000 200000 240000 FALSE 0 EQUALS `answered` TRUE
-- s 13A(4): a $610,000 purchase is within a $650,000 cap set by regulation.
#ASSERT `Is my transaction within the cap` `a contract for the purchase of a home` `1 Mar 2024` `it replaces no earlier contract` 610000 610000 0 0 TRUE 650000 EQUALS `answered` TRUE

§§ `ss 8 to 12 -- the eligibility criteria, one at a time`

-- s 8A(1), (2).
#ASSERT `Am I old enough` 18 FALSE
#ASSERT (NOT (`Am I old enough` 17 FALSE))
#ASSERT `Am I old enough` 17 TRUE

-- s 9(1), s 3 "permanent resident".
#ASSERT `Do I meet the citizenship or residency criterion` `an Australian citizen` FALSE `none of these` FALSE EQUALS `answered` TRUE
#ASSERT `Do I meet the citizenship or residency criterion` `the holder of a permanent visa` FALSE `none of these` FALSE EQUALS `answered` TRUE
#ASSERT `Do I meet the citizenship or residency criterion` `a New Zealand citizen holding a special category visa` FALSE `none of these` FALSE EQUALS `answered` TRUE
#ASSERT `Do I meet the citizenship or residency criterion` `none of these` FALSE `none of these` FALSE EQUALS `answered` FALSE
-- s 9(2): Tom (no qualifying visa) applying jointly with Priya (a citizen) is exempted.
#ASSERT `Do I meet the citizenship or residency criterion` `none of these` TRUE `an Australian citizen` FALSE EQUALS `answered` TRUE
-- s 9(2) needs joint applicants: a citizen spouse who is not applying does not help.
#ASSERT `Do I meet the citizenship or residency criterion` `none of these` FALSE `an Australian citizen` FALSE EQUALS `answered` FALSE
#ASSERT `Do I meet the citizenship or residency criterion` `none of these` TRUE `none of these` FALSE EQUALS `answered` FALSE
-- A further applicant is not asked about: not covered.
#ASSERT `Do I meet the citizenship or residency criterion` `none of these` FALSE `none of these` TRUE EQUALS `not covered` `the application has more applicants, spouses or de facto partners than this question asks about`

-- s 10(1): no earlier grant.
#ASSERT `Am I free of the second grant bar` `no` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `no` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `answered` TRUE
-- s 10(1): an earlier NSW grant, not paid back.
#ASSERT `Am I free of the second grant bar` `yes, in New South Wales` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `no` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `answered` FALSE
-- s 10(2): paid back with any s 45 penalty.
#ASSERT `Am I free of the second grant bar` `yes, in New South Wales` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `no` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `answered` TRUE
-- s 10(1)(a): a grant under a corresponding law (Queensland, say), not paid back.
#ASSERT `Am I free of the second grant bar` `yes, in another State or a Territory, and it counts under that place's law` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `no` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `answered` FALSE
-- s 10(1)(a): unsure whether that law corresponds: not covered.
#ASSERT `Am I free of the second grant bar` `yes, in another State or a Territory, and I am not sure whether it counts under that place's law` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `no` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not covered` `it turns on the corresponding law of another State or a Territory, which is not deposited`
-- s 10(2): unsure, but paid back: the bar is lifted whichever way the other law goes.
#ASSERT `Am I free of the second grant bar` `yes, in another State or a Territory, and I am not sure whether it counts under that place's law` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `no` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `answered` TRUE
-- s 10(1): Priya's husband Tom had a NSW grant in 2010, not paid back.
#ASSERT `Am I free of the second grant bar` `no` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE `yes, in New South Wales` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `answered` FALSE
-- s 6(2): the same, but they separated for good, as the Chief Commissioner is satisfied: Tom is not her spouse.
#ASSERT `Am I free of the second grant bar` `no` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE `yes, in New South Wales` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `answered` TRUE
-- s 6(1)(b): a de facto partner's unrepaid grant counts too.
#ASSERT `Am I free of the second grant bar` `no` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE `yes, in New South Wales` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `answered` FALSE
-- A definite bar settles it, whatever an uncertain interstate grant of the partner turns out to be.
#ASSERT `Am I free of the second grant bar` `yes, in New South Wales` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE `yes, in another State or a Territory, and I am not sure whether it counts under that place's law` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `answered` FALSE

-- s 11: nothing held. The same answers fit an investment flat bought in 2015 and never lived in: s 11(3) needs 6 months'
-- residence, so it does not count.
#ASSERT `Have I never held a home that counts` `no` `no` FALSE FALSE FALSE `no` `no` FALSE EQUALS `answered` TRUE
-- s 11(1)(a): held a relevant interest in NSW residential property before 1 July 2000, lived in it or not.
#ASSERT `Have I never held a home that counts` `yes, in New South Wales` `no` FALSE FALSE FALSE `no` `no` FALSE EQUALS `answered` FALSE
-- s 11(1)(b): the same elsewhere, counting under the corresponding law.
#ASSERT `Have I never held a home that counts` `yes, in another State or a Territory, and it counts under that place's law` `no` FALSE FALSE FALSE `no` `no` FALSE EQUALS `answered` FALSE
-- s 11(1)(b): unsure whether it counts there: not covered.
#ASSERT `Have I never held a home that counts` `yes, in another State or a Territory, and I am not sure whether it counts under that place's law` `no` FALSE FALSE FALSE `no` `no` FALSE EQUALS `not covered` `it turns on the corresponding law of another State or a Territory, which is not deposited`
-- s 11(3): owned a NSW home since 2000 and lived in it for 6 months.
#ASSERT `Have I never held a home that counts` `no` `yes, in New South Wales` FALSE FALSE FALSE `no` `no` FALSE EQUALS `answered` FALSE
-- s 11(3): a de facto partner's 6 months in a home she owned count against him.
#ASSERT `Have I never held a home that counts` `no` `no` FALSE TRUE FALSE `no` `yes, in New South Wales` FALSE EQUALS `answered` FALSE

-- s 12: Jess, completion 15 August 2025, moves in 1 September 2025 and stays 24 months.
#ASSERT `Do I meet the residence requirement` `15 Aug 2025` TRUE `1 Sep 2025` 24 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `1 Sep 2025` 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `answered` TRUE
-- s 12(1)(a): moving in on 15 August 2026 is within 12 months; on 16 August 2026 it is not.
#ASSERT `Do I meet the residence requirement` `15 Aug 2025` TRUE `15 Aug 2026` 12 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `1 Sep 2025` 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `answered` TRUE
#ASSERT `Do I meet the residence requirement` `15 Aug 2025` TRUE `16 Aug 2026` 12 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `1 Sep 2025` 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `answered` FALSE
-- s 12(3)(a): the late start approved.
#ASSERT `Do I meet the residence requirement` `15 Aug 2025` TRUE `16 Aug 2026` 12 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `1 Sep 2025` 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `answered` TRUE
-- s 12(1)(b): 11 months; (3)(b) a shorter stay approved.
#ASSERT `Do I meet the residence requirement` `15 Aug 2025` TRUE `1 Sep 2025` 11 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `1 Sep 2025` 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `answered` FALSE
#ASSERT `Do I meet the residence requirement` `15 Aug 2025` TRUE `1 Sep 2025` 11 FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `1 Sep 2025` 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `answered` TRUE
-- s 12(4): never lives there, but exempted.
#ASSERT `Do I meet the residence requirement` `15 Aug 2025` FALSE `1 Sep 2025` 0 FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE `1 Sep 2025` 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `answered` TRUE
-- s 12(6): Priya never lives there, but Tom, applying with her, does for 18 months.
#ASSERT `Do I meet the residence requirement` `20 Mar 2026` FALSE `1 Apr 2026` 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE `1 Apr 2026` 18 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `answered` TRUE
-- s 12(6) needs joint applicants: a partner who lives there but is not applying does not help.
#ASSERT `Do I meet the residence requirement` `20 Mar 2026` FALSE `1 Apr 2026` 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE `1 Apr 2026` 18 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `answered` FALSE

§§ `ss 7, 8 to 12, 18 -- the whole application`

