§§ `s 18 -- the amount`

-- s 18(1)(b): commencement on or after 1 January 2016: $10,000.
#ASSERT `How much is the grant for my transaction` `a contract for the purchase of a home` `1 Mar 2024` `it replaces no earlier contract` FALSE 580000 EQUALS `answered` 10000
#ASSERT `How much is the grant for my transaction` `a contract for the purchase of a home` `1 Jan 2016` `it replaces no earlier contract` FALSE 580000 EQUALS `answered` 10000
-- s 18(1)(a): from 1 October 2012 to 31 December 2015: $15,000.
#ASSERT `How much is the grant for my transaction` `a contract for the purchase of a home` `31 Dec 2015` `it replaces no earlier contract` FALSE 580000 EQUALS `answered` 15000
#ASSERT `How much is the grant for my transaction` `a contract for the purchase of a home` `1 Oct 2012` `it replaces no earlier contract` FALSE 580000 EQUALS `answered` 15000
#ASSERT `How much is the grant for my transaction` `a contract for the purchase of a home` `1 Dec 2014` `it replaces no earlier contract` FALSE 580000 EQUALS `answered` 15000
-- Schedule 1 cl 18: before 1 October 2012: not covered.
#ASSERT `How much is the grant for my transaction` `a contract for the purchase of a home` `30 Sep 2012` `it replaces no earlier contract` FALSE 580000 EQUALS `not covered` `the commencement date is before 1 October 2012, and Schedule 1 Part 11 keeps the earlier Part 2, which is not deposited`
-- s 18(2): a contract made on 5 October 2012 under an option granted in the transitional period: $7,000.
#ASSERT `How much is the grant for my transaction` `a contract for the purchase of a home` `5 Oct 2012` `it replaces no earlier contract` TRUE 580000 EQUALS `answered` 7000
-- s 18(2): the same, though the option is exercised in March 2016: still $7,000, not $10,000.
#ASSERT `How much is the grant for my transaction` `a comprehensive home building contract` `5 Mar 2016` `it replaces no earlier contract` TRUE 330000 EQUALS `answered` 7000
-- s 18(2) reaches only a purchase or a building contract: an owner build in 2014 gets $15,000.
#ASSERT `How much is the grant for my transaction` `the building of a home by an owner builder` `1 Dec 2014` `it replaces no earlier contract` TRUE 300000 EQUALS `answered` 15000
-- s 18(4): the grant is at most the consideration: an owner builder whose costs are $8,000 gets $8,000.
#ASSERT `How much is the grant for my transaction` `the building of a home by an owner builder` `1 Mar 2024` `it replaces no earlier contract` FALSE 8000 EQUALS `answered` 8000
-- s 13(3A), Schedule 1 cl 19: a replacement of a pre-October 2012 contract: not covered.
#ASSERT `How much is the grant for my transaction` `a contract for the purchase of a home` `1 Mar 2024` `it replaces a contract made before 1 October 2012` FALSE 580000 EQUALS `not covered` `the Chief Commissioner is satisfied the contract replaces one made before 1 July 2017, and Schedule 1 keeps the earlier law, which is not encoded`

§§ `s 14(5), (6) -- when to apply`

-- s 14(5)(b): 12 months after completion on 15 August 2025.
#ASSERT `By when must I apply` `15 Aug 2025` EQUALS `15 Aug 2026`
-- READING: completion on 29 February 2028 gives 28 February 2029.
#ASSERT `By when must I apply` `29 Feb 2028` EQUALS `28 Feb 2029`
-- s 14(5)(a): from the commencement date itself; not the day before, unless allowed (s 14(6)).
#ASSERT `Is my application in time` `1 Mar 2024` `15 Aug 2025` `1 Mar 2024` FALSE
#ASSERT (NOT (`Is my application in time` `1 Mar 2024` `15 Aug 2025` `28 Feb 2024` FALSE))
-- s 14(5)(b): the last day, and the day after; s 14(6) the Chief Commissioner allows it.
#ASSERT `Is my application in time` `1 Mar 2024` `15 Aug 2025` `15 Aug 2026` FALSE
#ASSERT (NOT (`Is my application in time` `1 Mar 2024` `15 Aug 2025` `16 Aug 2026` FALSE))
#ASSERT `Is my application in time` `1 Mar 2024` `15 Aug 2025` `16 Aug 2026` TRUE

§§ `ss 20, 21 -- conditions of an advance payment`

-- s 20(2): paid before completion on a contract of 1 March 2024 that is still not completed: must notify and repay.
#ASSERT `Must I repay because my transaction was not completed in time` TRUE `1 Mar 2024` FALSE `1 Mar 2024` FALSE `1 Mar 2024`
-- Completed on 20 February 2025, within 12 months: no.
#ASSERT (NOT (`Must I repay because my transaction was not completed in time` TRUE `1 Mar 2024` TRUE `20 Feb 2025` FALSE `1 Mar 2024`))
-- Completed on 1 March 2025, the last day of the 12 months: no.
#ASSERT (NOT (`Must I repay because my transaction was not completed in time` TRUE `1 Mar 2024` TRUE `1 Mar 2025` FALSE `1 Mar 2024`))
-- Completed on 15 March 2025, after the 12 months: yes; but not if the Chief Commissioner allowed until 30 June 2025.
#ASSERT `Must I repay because my transaction was not completed in time` TRUE `1 Mar 2024` TRUE `15 Mar 2025` FALSE `1 Mar 2024`
#ASSERT (NOT (`Must I repay because my transaction was not completed in time` TRUE `1 Mar 2024` TRUE `15 Mar 2025` TRUE `30 Jun 2025`))
-- Not paid early: the s 20(2) condition does not arise.
#ASSERT (NOT (`Must I repay because my transaction was not completed in time` FALSE `1 Mar 2024` FALSE `1 Mar 2024` FALSE `1 Mar 2024`))
-- s 20(2): the period ends 1 March 2025; notice and repayment by 15 March 2025; with a longer period to 30 June 2025, by
-- 14 July 2025.
#ASSERT `By when must I repay if my transaction is not completed in time` `1 Mar 2024` FALSE `1 Mar 2024` EQUALS `15 Mar 2025`
#ASSERT `By when must I repay if my transaction is not completed in time` `1 Mar 2024` TRUE `30 Jun 2025` EQUALS `14 Jul 2025`
-- s 20(2A): aware on 3 November 2025 that the value is over the cap: by 17 November 2025.
#ASSERT `By when must I repay because my transaction is over the cap` `3 Nov 2025` EQUALS `17 Nov 2025`
-- s 20(3): paid in anticipation; Jess leaves after 7 months: must notify and repay. Staying 24 months: no. Not paid in
-- anticipation: no.
#ASSERT `Must I repay because I did not meet the residence requirement` TRUE `15 Aug 2025` TRUE `1 Sep 2025` 7 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `1 Sep 2025` 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `answered` TRUE
#ASSERT `Must I repay because I did not meet the residence requirement` TRUE `15 Aug 2025` TRUE `1 Sep 2025` 24 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `1 Sep 2025` 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `answered` FALSE
#ASSERT `Must I repay because I did not meet the residence requirement` FALSE `15 Aug 2025` TRUE `1 Sep 2025` 7 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `1 Sep 2025` 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `answered` FALSE
-- s 12(6): Jess leaves after 7 months, but her co-applicant stays 12: the requirement is met, nothing to repay.
#ASSERT `Must I repay because I did not meet the residence requirement` TRUE `15 Aug 2025` TRUE `1 Sep 2025` 7 FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE `1 Sep 2025` 12 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `answered` FALSE
-- s 20(3), READING (finding 11): moved in on 1 September 2025, so the period ends 1 September 2026; by 15 September 2026.
#ASSERT `By when must I repay if I do not meet the residence requirement` `15 Aug 2025` TRUE `1 Sep 2025` FALSE EQUALS `15 Sep 2026`
-- Never moved in: the period ends 12 months after completion, 15 August 2026; by 29 August 2026.
#ASSERT `By when must I repay if I do not meet the residence requirement` `15 Aug 2025` FALSE `1 Sep 2025` FALSE EQUALS `29 Aug 2026`
-- Moved in too late without approval: the same; with a s 12(3)(a) approval of the 1 October 2026 start, 15 October 2027.
#ASSERT `By when must I repay if I do not meet the residence requirement` `15 Aug 2025` TRUE `1 Oct 2026` FALSE EQUALS `29 Aug 2026`
#ASSERT `By when must I repay if I do not meet the residence requirement` `15 Aug 2025` TRUE `1 Oct 2026` TRUE EQUALS `15 Oct 2027`
-- s 20(4), s 21(4): 50 penalty units.
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined for breaking a condition` EQUALS 50

§§ `s 45 -- what can be recovered`

-- s 45(1)(a), (b) and the s 20 conditions.
#ASSERT `Can I be made to repay the grant` TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I be made to repay the grant` FALSE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I be made to repay the grant` FALSE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT (NOT (`Can I be made to repay the grant` FALSE FALSE FALSE))
-- Paid $10,000 in error, no dishonesty, no failure to repay: $10,000 and no penalty (s 45(2) has no ground).
#ASSERT `What is the most that can be recovered from me` 10000 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS 10000
-- A s 20 condition required repayment and it was not made: $10,000 plus a penalty of up to $10,000 (s 45(2)(c)(ii)).
#ASSERT `What is the most that can be recovered from me` 10000 FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS 20000
-- Paid as a result of dishonesty, the decision reversed: $10,000 plus up to $10,000 (s 45(1)(b), (2)(a)).
#ASSERT `What is the most that can be recovered from me` 10000 FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS 20000
-- No ground to require repayment: nothing, and no penalty, since it cannot exceed the amount to be repaid.
#ASSERT `What is the most that can be recovered from me` 10000 FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS 0

§§ `The core, on records`

-- s 8: a company cannot apply; the core's criterion fails though every other criterion is met.
`a company applying` MEANS
    `Applicant` WITH
        `is a natural person`               IS FALSE
        `age when applying`                 IS 30
        `exempted from the age requirement` IS FALSE
        `status`                            IS `an Australian citizen`
        `the applicant's history`           IS `a history from` `no` FALSE `no` `no`
        `the applicant's partners`          IS EMPTY
        `the applicant's residence`         IS `a residence from` TRUE `1 Sep 2025` 24 FALSE FALSE FALSE

`Jess's transaction` MEANS `a transaction from` `a contract for the purchase of a home` TRUE `1 Mar 2024` `15 Aug 2025` TRUE `neither renovated nor built to replace demolished premises` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE `it replaces no earlier contract` FALSE 580000 580000 0 0 FALSE 0 FALSE

GIVEN `applicants` IS A LIST OF `Applicant`
GIVETH AN `Application`
`an application by` `applicants` MEANS
    `Application` WITH
        `the applicants`                                                  IS `applicants`
        `the transaction`                                                 IS `Jess's transaction`
        `the largest ownership share of an owner who is not applying`     IS 0
        `the total ownership share of all small interest holders`         IS 0
        `the Chief Commissioner has authorised payment before completion` IS FALSE

GIVEN `status` IS A `Status on the commencement date`
GIVETH AN `Applicant`
`a person with status` `status` MEANS `an applicant from` 30 FALSE `status` (`a history from` `no` FALSE `no` `no`) EMPTY (`a residence from` TRUE `1 Sep 2025` 24 FALSE FALSE FALSE)

#ASSERT `the grant is payable on` (`an application by` (LIST `a company applying`)) EQUALS `answered` FALSE
-- s 7(1)(a): an application with no applicant at all is not payable.
#ASSERT `the grant is payable on` (`an application by` EMPTY) EQUALS `answered` FALSE
-- s 9(2) with three joint applicants, one a citizen: "at least one (but not all)" complies, so all are exempted.
#ASSERT `the grant is payable on` (`an application by` (LIST `a person with status` `none of these`, `a person with status` `an Australian citizen`, `a person with status` `none of these`)) EQUALS `answered` TRUE
#ASSERT `the grant is payable on` (`an application by` (LIST `a person with status` `none of these`, `a person with status` `none of these`, `a person with status` `none of these`)) EQUALS `answered` FALSE
-- s 14(5): from 1 March 2024 to 15 August 2026 is 897 days (365 + 365 + 167).
#ASSERT `the days from` `1 Mar 2024` `to` (`the application period ends on` `Jess's transaction`) EQUALS 897
-- s 20(2): the 12 months from 1 March 2024 end on 1 March 2025.
#ASSERT `the period for completion ends on` `Jess's transaction` `or` NOTHING EQUALS `1 Mar 2025`

§§ `Regulative rules`

-- s 14(5): Jess applies on day 400 of the 897-day application period.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 14(5), (6) -- an application may only be made within the application period` (`applicant` 1) 897 FALSE) 0 (LIST (EVENT (`applicant` 1) `apply for the grant` 400)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: BREACH BY applicant 1, "s 14(5): the application period has ended ..." (she applies on day 898)
#TRACE `s 14(5), (6) -- an application may only be made within the application period` (`applicant` 1) 897 FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `applicant` 1 DOES `apply for the grant` AT 898
-- s 14(6): the Chief Commissioner allows a late application; applying on day 950 is fine.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 14(5), (6) -- an application may only be made within the application period` (`applicant` 1) 897 TRUE) 0 (LIST (EVENT (`applicant` 1) `apply for the grant` 950)) EQUALS FULFILLED

-- s 20(2), s 21(3): Priya and Tom; Tom gives the notice on day 3, Priya repays on day 14: both conditions met for both.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 20(2) -- paid before completion, and not completed in time: give notice and repay within 14 days` 2 TRUE TRUE) 0 (LIST (EVENT (`applicant` 2) `give the Chief Commissioner written notice` 3), (EVENT (`applicant` 1) `repay the amount of the grant` 14)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: the repayment branch BREACHED BY applicant 2 OR applicant 1 (notice given on day 3, nobody repaid by day 14)
#TRACE `s 20(2) -- paid before completion, and not completed in time: give notice and repay within 14 days` 2 TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `applicant` 2 DOES `give the Chief Commissioner written notice` AT 3
    (WAITUNTIL 15)
-- Completed in time: no condition arises.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 20(2) -- paid before completion, and not completed in time: give notice and repay within 14 days` 2 TRUE FALSE) 0 EMPTY EQUALS FULFILLED

-- s 20(2A): Jess gives notice on day 5 and repays on day 10.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 20(2A) -- paid in anticipation of the cap, and over it: give notice and repay within 14 days` 1 TRUE TRUE) 0 (LIST (EVENT (`applicant` 1) `give the Chief Commissioner written notice` 5), (EVENT (`applicant` 1) `repay the amount of the grant` 10)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: BREACH BY applicant 1 on the repayment (repaid on day 15)
#TRACE `s 20(2A) -- paid in anticipation of the cap, and over it: give notice and repay within 14 days` 1 TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `applicant` 1 DOES `give the Chief Commissioner written notice` AT 5
    PARTY `applicant` 1 DOES `repay the amount of the grant` AT 15

-- s 20(3): not complied with; notice day 1, repayment day 2. Complied with: nothing arises.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 20(3) -- paid in anticipation of residence, and not complied with: give notice and repay within 14 days` 1 TRUE TRUE) 0 (LIST (EVENT (`applicant` 1) `give the Chief Commissioner written notice` 1), (EVENT (`applicant` 1) `repay the amount of the grant` 2)) EQUALS FULFILLED
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 20(3) -- paid in anticipation of residence, and not complied with: give notice and repay within 14 days` 1 TRUE FALSE) 0 EMPTY EQUALS FULFILLED

-- s 21(2), (3): a condition with 7 days for notice and 30 for repayment; applicant 1 notifies on day 7, applicant 2 repays
-- on day 30.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 21(2), (3) -- a condition imposed by the Chief Commissioner: give notice and repay within the stated periods` 2 TRUE 7 30) 0 (LIST (EVENT (`applicant` 1) `give the Chief Commissioner written notice` 7), (EVENT (`applicant` 2) `repay the amount of the grant` 30)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: the notice branch BREACHED BY applicant 2 OR applicant 1 (notice on day 8, after the 7 days)
#TRACE `s 21(2), (3) -- a condition imposed by the Chief Commissioner: give notice and repay within the stated periods` 2 TRUE 7 30 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `applicant` 1 DOES `give the Chief Commissioner written notice` AT 8
    PARTY `applicant` 2 DOES `repay the amount of the grant` AT 20

-- s 45(1): paid in error; the Chief Commissioner gives notice requiring repayment.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 45(1) -- the Chief Commissioner may require repayment by written notice` TRUE FALSE) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the Chief Commissioner` `require repayment by written notice` 10)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- s 45(2)(c)(ii): Jess did not repay $10,000 as a condition required; a $10,000 penalty is within the power.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 45(2) -- the Chief Commissioner may impose a penalty up to the amount to be repaid` 10000 FALSE TRUE) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the Chief Commissioner` (`impose a penalty` 10000) 5)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: the permission still open (a $12,000 penalty exceeds the $10,000 to be repaid and does not match it)
#TRACE `s 45(2) -- the Chief Commissioner may impose a penalty up to the amount to be repaid` 10000 FALSE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Chief Commissioner` DOES `impose a penalty` 12000 AT 5
